==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*maga-'' ‘kin’.  Cognate with [[Middle Dutch]] ''[[maech]]'' (Dutch [[maag]]), [[Old High German]] ''[[māg]]'', Gothic [[𐌼𐌴𐌲𐍃]] ‘son-in-law’.

